 (libraries tfl test_support qcheck-core qcheck-core.runner))

(test
 (name test_render)
 (modules test_render)
 (libraries tfl test_support qcheck-core qcheck-core.runner))

; The oracle fuzz suites (1.11): engine vs the 1.10 semantics, no Node
; involved. Default 1,000 iterations under `dune test`; the 20k gate is run
; explicitly with `-n 20000`.

(test
 (name test_oracle)
 (modules test_oracle)
 (libraries tfl test_support qcheck-core unix))

; The curated paper-cases audit (1.13): expectations from the literature, not
; from the engine. Pure engine calls, no Node, no fuzzing.

(test
 (name paper_cases)
 (modules paper_cases)
 (libraries tfl test_support))

; Robustness (1.14): the total Safe API under adversarial input, plus the
; pinned find_cancellation work-cap probe. No Node involved.

(test
 (name test_safe)
 (modules test_safe)
 (libraries tfl test_support qcheck-core qcheck-core.runner unix))

; The verification API (3.1): JSON round-trips, the Unknown ≠ Invalid
; contract, and the Safe.parse_program depth cap.

(test
 (name test_verify)
 (modules test_verify)
 (libraries tfl tfl_verify test_support yojson))

; The verification suite (3.2): ≥30 arguments through the public API,
; expectations shared with paper_cases so the two suites agree.

(test
 (name test_verify_cases)
 (modules test_verify_cases)
 (libraries tfl_verify test_support))

; The .env loader (2.1): key handling for the OpenRouter client.

(test
 (name test_env)
 (modules test_env)
 (libraries translate unix))

; The OpenRouter client's failure handling (4.9): what counts as retryable,
; that the loop acts on it, and the cost ceiling. No network — an empty 200
; body classified as fatal is what silently dropped 22 sentences from the
; 2026-08-02 fidelity run.

(test
 (name test_llm_client)
 (modules test_llm_client)
 (libraries translate lwt lwt.unix))

; The translation contract (4.1): the validator against good and bad payloads.

(test
 (name test_schema)
 (modules test_schema)
 (libraries translate test_support yojson))

; The translation prompt (4.2): every few-shot formula parses through the
; engine, and the notation coverage the few-shot set teaches is still intact.

(test
 (name test_prompts)
 (modules test_prompts)
 (libraries tfl translate test_support))

; The translator harness (4.3): the classification step, no network. Guards
; misattribution — pairing a formula with the wrong sentence is silent and
; nothing downstream can detect it.

(test
 (name test_translator)
 (modules test_translator)
 (libraries tfl translate test_support))

; The fidelity gold set: the measuring instrument for the translation
; experiment. A wrong entry is worse than no measurement — every downstream
; number still computes and the result is fiction. Guards unparseable gold,
; wrong stated verdicts, and contamination from the few-shot prompt.

(test
 (name test_fidelity_set)
 (modules test_fidelity_set)
 (libraries tfl tfl_verify translate test_support yojson)
 (deps ../data/fidelity/items.jsonl))

; The fidelity scorer (4.5b). It decides the headline number, so both failure
; directions are pinned: too strict punishes an arbitrary stem choice, too
; loose lets a converted A-form score as correct.

(test
 (name test_score)
 (modules test_score)
 (libraries tfl bench test_support))

; The back-check (4.4), offline half. The first test decides whether the
; mechanism can work at all: if a meaning-inverting formula renders into the
; same English as the correct one, no judge could ever catch it.

(test
 (name test_backcheck)
 (modules test_backcheck)
 (libraries tfl tfl_verify translate test_support))
